# Repository Registry

All `jssturm` GitHub repos are tracked in `.cursor/repos/registry.json`.

**Push skip list:** `.cursor/repos/push-skip-list.json` — upstream fork clones (`zoo-flow`, `agenttrace-luo`, `bernstein`, `omniroute`) must never be pushed. See `zoo-git-push-skip-list.mdc`.

**Disregard list:** `.cursor/repos/disregard-list.json` — repos never treated as clone targets or reported as missing (renamed/deleted upstream, or intentionally untracked). Currently: `cv-santiago`. Enforced by `clone` (default) and `list --missing`; an explicit `clone <name>` still overrides it.

## Commands

```bash
node scripts/inventory-repos.mjs          # refresh registry
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs list        # all repos
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs list --missing
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs list --needs-zoo
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs clone       # clone missing (GITHUB_TOKEN or gh auth)
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs sync        # fetch all + fast-forward clean repos
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs sync --dry-run     # report drift, change nothing
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs scrub-remotes      # strip credentials from .git/config
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs propagate-zoo
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs propagate-full   # auto-runs sanitize-public + verify
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs verify-public
node scripts/manage-repos.mjs sanitize-public
```

## Staying current with cloud work

Cloud-agent work lands on `origin/cursor/*` branches and merges to `main` remotely. Local clones drift silently until fetched.

Run `sync` before starting work in any repo, or after cloud agents finish.

`sync` guarantees:
- Fetches every clone with `--prune`, including the four fetch-only fork clones
- Fast-forwards **only** a clean tree with zero local commits — the sole lossless case
- **Never** merges, rebases, or pushes; diverged and dirty repos are reported, not touched
- Lists `origin/cursor/*` branches so cloud-agent work is visible

## Credential hygiene

**Never embed a token in a remote URL.** `git clone https://<token>@github.com/...` persists the token into `.git/config` permanently, where it leaks via `git remote -v` and breaks every clone on rotation.

Auth comes from the git credential helper, or from `GITHUB_TOKEN` supplied per-invocation through an ephemeral credential helper. Run `scrub-remotes` if any remote acquires inline credentials.

## Full GitHub capture

Credentials load automatically from `development/.env` (see `.env.example`):

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # add GITHUB_TOKEN
node scripts/inventory-repos.mjs
```

Or use `gh auth login` if GitHub CLI is installed.

## Tier policy

| Tier | Examples | Zoo action |
|------|----------|------------|
| strategic (private) | Project-Athena, Elevated-Applicant | Full overlay + Athena doctrine |
| owned-local (private) | trading-bot, LexiRoute | full or slim bundle; Athena at hub only |
| public | Plan-It, elevated-installer, forks | **Sanitized** — no Athena; `sanitize-public` |
| owned-remote | cv-santiago | clone first |

**Athena is proprietary.** Never propagate `zoo-athena-doctrine.mdc` to public repos.

